---
layout: base.njk
useSolverCSS: true
useReactSolvers: true
# The solver is the whole page here, not a widget inside a guide: its CSS and
# bundle are the critical path, so base.njk preloads the bundle and lets the
# stylesheet block paint. guide-with-solver.njk deliberately does not set this.
solverIsPrimary: true
skipTOC: true
---
<div class="solver-only-page">
{#- A solver page is nearly always an arrival, not a step: readers land on
    "Terminus Beamsmasher Solver" straight from search, solve their one puzzle
    and leave, because nothing on the page points at the guide the solver
    belongs to. The return pill can't cover this — it only appears for someone
    who clicked through from the guide in the first place. This link is always
    there, which also gives every solver page a crawlable edge back into its
    parent guide instead of dead-ending the link graph.

    Outside any .content-container and not a <p>, so line-flagger.ts leaves it
    alone: this is chrome, not a line of the guide anyone would report. -#}
{#- Four solver pages point at a guide that is still an "unfinished" stub
    (Totenreich, Shattered Veil, Reckoning, Gorod Krovi as of writing), and
    those render a "Sorry, this page is not ready yet!" placeholder. Sending a
    reader there is worse than sending them nowhere, so the link waits until the
    guide is live. `unfinishedPages` is the index's own `a.disabled` registry,
    so the link appears the moment that class comes off — no second list to
    remember to update. -#}
{%- set guideClean = guideUrl | cleanUrl %}
{%- if mapName and guideUrl and guideClean not in unfinishedPages %}
{#- "Full Terminus Map Guide" reads fine; "Full The Frozen Dawn Map Guide" does
    not, and three maps carry a leading article. Those put the name first
    instead — same words, both orders grammatical, and the map name still opens
    the anchor text on the pages where it matters most. -#}
{%- set guideLabel = (mapName + ' Full Map Guide') if mapName.startsWith('The ') else ('Full ' + mapName + ' Map Guide') %}
<nav class="solver-guide-link" aria-label="Related guide">
    <a class="solver-guide-link__anchor internal-link" href="{{ guideClean }}">{{ guideLabel }}</a>
</nav>
{%- endif %}
{{ content | safe }}
</div>
